[Page:krakout-ii]
PageContent=#INCLUDE(KrakoutIIContent)

[KrakoutIIContent]
<h2 class="ref-section" id="the-release">The release</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
Krakout II is a 1988 modification of this game by Firefly Software of Poland
(<a href="https://spectrumcomputing.co.uk/entry/35831/ZX-Spectrum/Krakout_II">ZXDB entry 35831</a>).
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
Its #R$6754(level layouts) and some of its texts differ from this game's.
#R$B9D2(The routine that draws the object pool) differs in one byte. It skips an object whose Y is 175
or more, where this game skips one from Y 167.
</div>

<h2 class="ref-section" id="loading-screen">Loading screen</h2>

<img alt="Krakout II loading screen" src="images/krakout-ii-loading-screen.png" />

<h2 class="ref-section" id="the-texts">The texts</h2>

#TABLE(default,centre)
{ =h Text | =h Change }
{ The name in the highest-ranked #R$B67E(default high-score entry) | <div class="text-diff"><samp class="text-del">TOM WAITS</samp><samp class="text-ins">COMMUNARDS</samp></div> }
{ The menu's #R$BEDF(copyright line) | <div class="text-diff"><samp class="text-del">@ 1987 GREMLIN GRAPHICS.</samp><samp class="text-ins">@ 1988 FIREFLY SOFTWARE.</samp></div> }
{ The #R$C443(credits scroll) | <div class="text-diff"><samp class="text-del">KRAKOUT - SPECCY CONVERSION BY GREG HOLMES,ANDY GREEN - DESIGN BOB TOONE - GRAFIX TEZ LLOYD - NOT DROID  &amp; STEVIE WEEVIE KERRY - MUSIC BY BENN DAGLISH - THANKS TO SHAUN &amp; MAD PIERRE FOR THE POP HL'S HELLO TO CHIGLEY,CLISSY,BUCK,FUNGI,PINKY,MARCO AND A SPECIAL HELLO TO PSY THE HEROINE , NOT FORGETTING OUR RASTUS!  BY THE WAY THE SHIELD ONLY LASTS FOR 23 ALLIGATORS !!</samp><samp class="text-ins">* KRAKOUT 2++ * WITH MEGA TRAINER @ 1988 FIREFLY SOFTWARE LIMITED. WRITTEN BY BILL GILBERT IN 27TH APRIL ANNO DOMINI 1988. MEGA TRAINER BY PHONEX 1988. MEGA GREETINGS TO COLOR MAGIC. SPECIAL GREETINGS TO PHONEX,MARCIN,MACIEK,DAREK,PIOTREK,ALF,OLO,M AND Z,MAC,JAMES. NORMAL GREETINGS TO ALL HACKERS USERS SINCLAIR COMPUTER.</samp></div> }
TABLE#

<h2 class="ref-section" id="the-bricks">The bricks</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
Krakout II's levels place a brick design that this game's levels never place:
the angry face, in every ink. Its tiles and colors come from this game's
#R$921A(tile-glyph groups) and #R$9191(brick attributes), which Krakout II
leaves unchanged.
</div>

#UDGTABLE(default)
{ =h Design | =h Inks }
{ angry face | #UDGARRAY2,65,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD98;$DDA0;$DDA8;$DCA0)(krakout-ii-angry-face-1)#UDGARRAY2,66,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD98;$DDA0;$DDA8;$DCA0)(krakout-ii-angry-face-2)#UDGARRAY2,67,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD98;$DDA0;$DDA8;$DCA0)(krakout-ii-angry-face-3)#UDGARRAY2,68,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD98;$DDA0;$DDA8;$DCA0)(krakout-ii-angry-face-4)#UDGARRAY2,69,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD98;$DDA0;$DDA8;$DCA0)(krakout-ii-angry-face-5)#UDGARRAY2,70,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD98;$DDA0;$DDA8;$DCA0)(krakout-ii-angry-face-6)#UDGARRAY2,71,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DD98;$DDA0;$DDA8;$DCA0)(krakout-ii-angry-face-7) }
UDGTABLE#

<h2 class="ref-section" id="level-by-level">Level by level</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
One card per level, in level order, set as on the #LINK(Levels)(level set)
page. Each level keeps this game's #R$86F8(spawn cells) and #R$8888(wave script)
for its level index.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
Level 21's layout opens with an extra empty cell, which moves it and every
later layout one cell along. Read one cell later, the layouts of levels 21 to
100 form whole 9×9 designs. As the game draws them, each design sits one column
to the right, and its rightmost column wraps to the left edge one row down. Up to
level 99, a design's bottom-right cell falls into the next level's layout, where
the game draws it in the top-left cell. A brick in that cell is a stray from the
previous design. Level 100's bottom-right cell lies in the spawn-cell table, and
the game never draws it.
</div>

